cker hero he works at a  low-level electronics store he can't  remember his mother's birthday he hangs  out with his we dealing besties way too  much and he can't seem to commit to his  longtime girlfriend Liz when the dead  walking threatened to end humanity Shawn  finally steps up and sets out to save  the lives of everyone he loves by taking  them to his favorite pub and having a  drink while things blow over they  drinking during the apocalypse might  sound like a good idea but in Shawn's  case it's an absolute disaster even  setting aside that perilous road to get  to the Winchester matters get out of  hand quickly when Shawn and his crew  find their way inside and people start  to die not Shawn though he somehow finds  a way to safety and even manages to save  less still Shawn will be forced to live  the rest of his life with the blood of  those fallen companions on his hands  giving a whole new meaning to the phrase  you've got red on you here's a few  pointers for all of the lovers out there  who can't quite tell whether or not that  certain someone you've just met is the  one if you wake up in the middle of the  night and find them in your room  uninvited and watching you sleep it's  time to end that relationship if they  break up with you in the middle of the  woods and leave you there crying and  alone rather than giving you a ride home  you should stay broken up if they're  overprotective to the point of  threatening your friends just because  they're talking to you you might want to  take some space if they ever almost kill  you because they really really like the  taste of your blood you should probably  seek out the authorities and for pete's  sake if they turn to you after just a  few days and declare you are my life now  just go ahead and get us  draining order since Twilight hit  theaters in 2008 some of Edward Cullen's  sparkly sheen has lost its luster and  people are starting to see that he was  really just an undead creep and that  Bella's life would have been totally  fine if he had just left her alone  being a superhero means making enemies  and making enemies means the people you  love will always be in peril that's the  one lesson Peter Parker learns the hard  way and the amazing spider-man tear and  he learns it at the expense of his  girlfriend Gwen Stacy of course Peter  didn't have to learn that lesson at all  because he had someone explicitly lay  out the stakes of being a hero  Gwen's father police captain George  Stacy died while saving spider-man's  life with his dying words he had one  simple request but pizza not date his  daughter so she'd never be the target of  one of spider-man's enemies a last pizza  completely ignores it in the sequel so  it should come as no surprise that Gwen  is eventually taken hostage by the bad  guys and pays for Peters heroics with  her life if only someone had warned him  this exact thing would happen Oh Wayne
 

